      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've been experiencing this issue as well. Whenever I move around, and as soon as I stop moving, VRChat will instantly activate a gesture depending on the direction I was moving. Before the Avatars 3.0 update, this was not the case. Gestures used to only activate after retouching the trackpad or after a bit of a delay (and this older behavior is definitely preferred). I don't want to be sticking my tongue out or making surprised expressions every time I make any sort of little movement in-game... Imagine playing a game where WASD also activates a random voice command or something (in addition to moving you around). That's kinda what feels like is happening here... (Using Vive controllers, just to clarify)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-08-09T21:27:52.683Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Because of this new update. Me and as well a few of my friends that are either on Vive or Windows mixed with the touchpad to walk. We think it is annoying that everytime you walk and let go of the touchpad, a certain hand gesture goes off when we don't want to use the hand gesture. We know we can just turn off hand gestures, but we'd rather have gestures on. It would be really nice if the hand gestures can be fixed when using touchpad to walk.",
